@end example
@end quotation

@quotation
@strong{@anchor{Exercise 3.65}Exercise 3.65:} Use the series
@displaymath
\ln 2 \,=\, 1 - {1\over2} + {1\over3} - {1\over4} + \dots
@end displaymath
@ifinfo

@example
            1     1     1
ln 2 = 1 - --- + --- - --- + ...
            2     3     4
@end example

@end ifinfo
@noindent
to compute three sequences of approximations to the natural logarithm of 2, in
